- Camera lives here: `camera_shift` is a screen-pixel vector, `camera_zoom` an
- isotropic scalar. $mol_touch drives both from pointer, wheel and pinch.
$bog_vmap_app_pane $mol_view
	- Absolute address of the `web.js` of the sandbox module. The frame has no
	- address of its own, so the markup it is raised from names the bundle itself,
	- and a relative path would have nothing to resolve against in an opaque origin.
	scene_bundle \
	- Whole document of the frame, built out of `scene_bundle` in `pane.view.ts`.
	scene_html \
	- Absolute address of the `web.js` of the donor pack, sent down as `pack_set`.
	- Part of the key of the frame as well: a realm cannot unload a bundle, so a
	- different pack has to be a different frame, see section 5.
	pack_uri \
	doc_src \
	doc_css \
	- Canvas placement of free parts, world coordinates keyed by property name.
	- Never joined with `doc_css`: that one is the document, this one is the desk.
	- Two way: dragging a node on the canvas writes here.
	spots? *
	- Every picked node, in the order they were picked. The ONE pick the pane has:
	- a single selection is a set of one, and `primary()` is the last of them. The
	- band writes here, and so does an ordinary press, so there is one write path.
	picked? /string
	doc_js *
	doc_root \
	- Sources of the land libraries, compiled by the scene before the document.
	- On the bridge and not in `scene_uri`: a change of lands is a recompile, a
	- change of pack is a reload, see section 5.
	libs /$bog_vmap_bridge_part
	- Whether the overlay may be cut open under the picked part. The host turns
	- this off while something is carried from the palette: that gesture has no
	- pointer capture, so a release over the hole would land in the frame and the
	- host would never hear of the drop.
	hole_allowed true
	- Wires of the document and the wirable ports of each part's class, from the
	- owner. The pane draws them and writes back through the two events below; it
	- never touches the document itself.
	wires /$bog_vmap_lang_link
	part_ports* /$bog_vmap_app_wire_port
	link_add? null
	link_drop? null
	- Nodes that carry a `sub` of their own: an artboard, and anything laid out by
	- tree inside one. A drop inside one of these goes into the tree at a position,
	- see section 8; a drop anywhere else lands on the canvas by coordinates.
	containers /string
	- `flexDirection` the node declares, empty when it declares none. From the
	- document, which the host owns, and so a statement rather than a guess: the
	- boxes of the children say nothing when there are fewer than two of them.
	axis* \
	- A node put into the tree of a container. The pane owns the geometry of the
	- gesture and asks the owner to write the document, never writing it itself.
	tree_move? null
	- Labels of the wires on screen, by wire name, as the scene reports them.
	values? *
	- Handshakes seen from ONE frame, keyed by the key of that frame. A fresh frame
	- has said nothing yet, and reads zero here without anybody having to remember
	- to clear anything.
	handshake*? 0
	ready false
	- The scene owes an answer to something we sent and has stopped answering.
	- Set by the watchdog, cleared by the next message from the scene.
	stalled? false
	error_at*? \
	- Node the failure of a channel belongs to, empty when the scene could not
	- attribute it. Kept apart from the text so that the strip and the mark on the
	- canvas read the same report without either parsing the other's sentence.
	error_node*? \
	error \
	isolation \
	camera_shift? $mol_vector_2d<number> /
		0
		0
	camera_zoom? 1
	- Which frame is live. Bumped by `scene_restart`: a new key is a new frame
	- element, so a stuck scene is replaced rather than talked to. The address of
	- the pack goes into the key beside it, see `scene_key`.
	scene_generation? 0
	Scene* $bog_vmap_app_pane_frame
		html <= scene_html
	sub /
		<= Overlay $bog_vmap_app_pane_overlay
			style <= overlay_style *
			frames <= frames /string
			frame_style* <= frame_style* *
			press? <=> node_press? null
			move? <=> node_move? null
			release? <=> node_release? null
		- Above the overlay and outside its hole, so a wire crossing the picked part
		- is not cut. Takes no pointer: the press on a dot is the overlay's, by geometry.
		<= Wire $bog_vmap_app_wire
			lines <= wire_lines /$bog_vmap_app_wire_line
			dots <= wire_dots /$bog_vmap_app_wire_dot
			drag_geometry <= wire_drag_geometry \
		- Failures of the scene, each on the node it belongs to. Above everything,
		- because a node that threw is what the eye has to be sent to first.
		<= Marks $mol_view
			sub <= error_marks /$mol_view
	- A failure sits at the corner of the node that caused it, and carries the text
	- of the failure as its tooltip. Picture only: the overlay under it takes the press.
	Mark* $mol_view
		style <= mark_style* *
		attr *
			^
			title <= mark_hint* \
		sub /
			\!
	- Where the node in hand would land among the children of a container. Put into
	- `sub` only while a drop has somewhere to go, so an idle canvas costs no node.
	Insert $mol_view
		style <= insert_style *
	- The band drawn while a modified pointer sweeps the canvas. Topmost and here
	- rather than on the overlay for the same reason as the line above it.
	Band $mol_view
		style <= band_style *
	plugins /
		^
		<= Touch $mol_touch
			allow_draw false
			allow_pan true
			allow_zoom true
			pan? <=> camera_shift?
			zoom? <=> camera_zoom?

- Transparent gate over the frame. It swallows every pointer event and lets it
- bubble up to the pane, where $mol_touch listens: there are no editor modes, one
- layer takes every gesture. A click that does not move is relayed to the scene
- as `click_at`, and under the picked part the layer is cut open, so that one
- part at a time gets real events. Hover on any other part does not work, and
- that is the accepted price of the overlay owning the input.
-
- Selection is drawn HERE and not in the scene: the overlay belongs to the host,
- so no code inside the document can fake a selection frame or hide one, and the
- ring stays crisp because the camera scales the scene, not this layer.
- @see ../../ARCHITECTURE.md section 4
$bog_vmap_app_pane_overlay $mol_view
	frames /string
	frame_style* *
	press? null
	move? null
	release? null
	event *
		^
		pointerdown? <=> press? null
		pointermove? <=> move? null
		pointerup? <=> release? null
	- Ring around a picked node, one per node, keyed by its name. Put into `sub`
	- only for the nodes actually picked, so an empty canvas costs no node at all.
	- The handles sit outside the box, on the strip of overlay that still takes
	- the pointer, and say where the part can be taken hold of.
	Frame* $mol_view
		style <= frame_style* *
		sub /
			<= Handle_nw $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \nw
			<= Handle_ne $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \ne
			<= Handle_sw $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \sw
			<= Handle_se $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \se

- A grip at one corner of the ring. Picture only, like the ring: the press it
- marks is taken by the overlay under it.
$bog_vmap_app_pane_handle $mol_view
	corner \
	attr *
		^
		bog_vmap_app_pane_handle_corner <= corner

- `sandbox` goes FIRST: $mol_dom_render_attributes writes the object in key order,
- and an iframe that got its source before its sandbox is already loading
- unsandboxed. `srcdoc` is the last key of the base dictionary, so the attribute
- that raises the document is written after the one that isolates it.
-
- `src` is dropped outright, and dropped rather than emptied: an iframe with an
- empty `src` loads the page it stands on. `null` is how a dictionary of
- attributes says «not this one» — the renderer removes the attribute instead of
- writing it.
- @see ../../ARCHITECTURE.md section 4
$bog_vmap_app_pane_frame $mol_frame
	attr *
		sandbox \allow-scripts
		^
		src null
